      "quote": "Item B-1.8.1: ORDINARY ROCK: - Part of: Excavating trenches of required width for pipes cables etc. ... depth up to 1.5 Mtr."
    }
  ],
  "answer": "The basic rate for excavating a trench in ordinary rock for a pipe of 150 mm diameter (which falls in the \"exceeding 80 mm but not exceeding 300 mm\" category) is Rs. 429.00 per metre (S6). Because the trench depth is 2.5 m, it exceeds 1.5 m but does not exceed 3 m, so the extra of 104 % (S1) is applied over the basic rate. The total rate therefore becomes 100 % + 104 % = 204 % of the basic rate, i.e. 429 × 204 / 100 = Rs. 875.16 per metre. [S6][S1][S3]",
